From 30d05bd0c3a90404fc35296bd088ce4100b5b073 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:19:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] app, interface, support kits: fix what the static analysis
 found

- BString: CharacterEscape() and CharacterDeescape() working in place read
  their own buffer after _MakeWritable() had moved or freed it, whenever
  the string held a NUL (or the source pointed into the string). The source
  is copied first when it lies in the string's buffer.
- BUrl: the scheme check counted with an int8, which wrapped at 128 and read
  before the string.
- BApplication: Quit() on an unlocked application that never ran deleted
  it, and then unlocked it.
- BPasswordKey: the copy constructor did not copy.
- BChannelControl: growing the channel count copied that many bytes of the
  values and limits, not that many int32s.
- BColumnListView: dragging a column title right of the last column moved
  the column to the front, with an uninitialized left edge; it goes to the
  end now.
- BFont::StringWidth(), BTextView's context menu and BPrivateScreen used
  values that are unset when app_server refuses or undo is off.
- BMessage: a copy whose header could not be allocated was sent.
- BLayoutBuilder: a menu item that could not be added was deleted, and the
  builder went on with NULL; it throws, as AddMenu() does.
- BShape: copying an empty shape passed NULL to memcpy().
- SimpleLayouter, ComplexLayouter: out of memory, one used an item that was
  not in its list, the other could never notice the failure (|= on true).

Test: HaikuArmQemu's tools/analysis-fixes/afxtest, string-escape-in-place
(under the guarded heap), url-long-scheme, application-quit-unlocked,
password-key-copy, channel-count-grow, column-drag-past-last,
font-zero-size-width and shape-copy-empty.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0144-app-interface-support-kits-fix-what-the-static-analysis-foun.patch 9c238419041ab6128534c0db8189861bc7851e78ec972c5c16bfc9fa273f8d4b
